    "for screening-style assay quality assessment.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to look for**\n",
    "\n",
    "* `G ± SE` — should be in 0.7–1.3 with a small standard error. Outliers\n",
    "  are visible in the scatter plot.\n",
    "* `Q` — close to 1 means the probe's quantum yield is unchanged on\n",
    "  binding (typical when the dye is not at the binding interface).\n",
    "  Deviations |Q − 1| > 0.3 trigger a warning.\n",
    "* `A_free ± SE` — measured from substrate-only wells; should be close to\n",
    "  the lowest points of the titration.\n",
    "* `Z' factor` — > 0.5 is excellent for screening, 0–0.5 marginal,\n",
    "  ≤ 0 unreliable. Requires at least 2 substrate wells and 2 titration\n",
    "  wells at the highest [protein] (positive control).\n"
