    "## Step 4 — Fit a binding model\n",
    "\n",
    "For each condition, choose a model and run the fit.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Models**\n",
    "\n",
    "* `fp_quadratic` (default and recommended) — exact closed-form solution\n",
    "  that explicitly accounts for ligand depletion (Roehrl et al. 2004 eq\n",
    "  6; Jarmoskaite et al. 2020 eq 5).\n",
    "* `one_site` — simple hyperbolic; valid only when [L*] ≪ K_D.\n",
    "* `hill` — phenomenological model with a Hill coefficient n_H, useful\n",
    "  as a diagnostic for non-hyperbolic curves.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Defaults** — `A_free` is fixed to the value measured from substrate\n",
    "wells; `Q` is fixed to the empirical estimate from the titration extremes;\n",
    "`Dl` (= [L*]) is fixed to the value entered in Step 2. `Kd` and `A_bound`\n",
    "are free. You can override initial values, set bounds, or fix parameters\n",
    "via the controls.\n",
    "\n",
    "Use **Run fit** to fit one condition at a time, or **Fit all conditions**\n",
    "to fit all of them with the current settings.\n"
   ]
